# MIDI with a DAW. Its clock: the tempo from the ticks' own times, to a tenth of a BPM. SONG POSITION then
# CONTINUE (a DAW's locate, its loop): the clock and the loop carry on from there. CCs in move the controls
# (HOME's, the throws, PAN, the FX page) and nothing echoes back; a knob turned sends its CC. Program
# changes both ways: scenes, journeys. The white keys go out as VOX's notes on the channel, the black keys
# as notes 36.. on the next; those notes in press the black keys. (The loop's notes do not go out: the
# hands' did, as they were played.)
autoplay 0
wait 300
dswell 0
tap REC
wait 100
key w2 down
wait 1000
key w2 up
wait 500
key w4 down
wait 500
key w4 up
wait 600
tap REC
wait 100
expect looplen 16
tap SEQ
wait 500
expect playing 0
clockin 90 8000
wait 400
expect ext 1
midi F2 04 00
midi FB
wait 500
expect playing 1
expect steps >5
expect steps <10
expect loop_pos >5
expect loop_pos <10
midi FC
wait 100
midi F2 0A 00
midi FB
wait 300
expect loop_pos >10
expect loop_pos <14
wait 3000
expect tempo_x10 >898
expect tempo_x10 <902
midi FC
wait 1500
clockin 133 4000
wait 3500
expect tempo_x10 >1327
expect tempo_x10 <1333
wait 1000
expect ext 0
midi B0 0E 7F
midi B0 55 00
midi B0 15 64
midi B0 66 20
wait 100
expect macro1 127
expect pan0 0
expect thr3 73
expect fx0 32
expect ccs_out 0
turn K2 2
wait 100
expect macro2 68
expect cc_out15 68
expect ccs_out 2
tapkey w2
wait 100
expect notes_out1 3
tapkey b0
wait 100
expect notes_out2 1
expect note_out 36
expect drone1 1
midi 91 24 7F
wait 100
midi 81 24 00
wait 100
expect drone1 0
expect notes_out2 1
turn PRESET 1
wait 100
expect pc_out 1
midi C0 09
wait 300
expect journey 2
expect pc_out 1
